    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87615" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προκαθ-ίημι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>let down beforehand,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὴν βαλανοδόκην βρόχον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aen.Tact.
					18.9
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ταραχὴν π. πόλιν</span>
			<i>plunge</i> the city into confusion, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				14.5
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τινὰ ἐξαπατᾶν</span>
			<i>put</i> a person <i>forward</i> in order to deceive, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				19.77
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὸν λόγον, τὴν δόξαν,</span>
			<i>spread</i> it <i>before,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				58.9
			</span></i>(prob.), <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				1.482J.
			</span></i>:— 
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τῷ ὕδατι τὰ σκεύη προκαθεῖτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					62.15
				</span></i>
			.</div>
